feat(ocale): expose per-locale localization on game-passes

Adds a `localization` Operation Group on `GamePassesClient` mirroring
the surface shipped on `DeveloperProductsClient` (#328):

- `localization.updateNameDescription({ gamePassId, languageCode,
  name?, description? })` PATCHes
  `/legacy-game-internationalization/v1/game-passes/{id}/name-description/language-codes/{lang}`,
  resolving to `Result<undefined>` so callers chain `get` themselves
  if they need post-update state. Idempotent — retries on 5xx.
- `localization.uploadIcon({ gamePassId, languageCode, image })`
  POSTs the multipart icon to
  `/legacy-game-internationalization/v1/game-passes/{id}/icons/language-codes/{lang}`,
  resolving to `Result<undefined>`. Does not retry on 5xx so a server
  failure mid-write cannot duplicate the asset.

Both methods queue against a shared `game-pass-localization`
operation key (100/min, sourced from the legacy
`gameinternationalization` service-wide cap) and a 401/403 from
upstream surfaces as a `PermissionError` naming
`legacy-game-pass:manage`. Closes #225.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
